#!/bin/sh
# Robotrac Maven Wrapper for macOS/Linux (Windows users: use mvnw.cmd).
# Downloads the Maven version named in .mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties once
# into ~/.m2/wrapper/dists and runs it.
set -e
BASEDIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
PROPS="$BASEDIR/.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties"
DIST_URL=$(grep '^distributionUrl=' "$PROPS" | cut -d= -f2-)
DIST_ZIP=$(basename "$DIST_URL")
DIST_NAME=${DIST_ZIP%-bin.zip}
DIST_ROOT="$HOME/.m2/wrapper/dists"
MAVEN_HOME_DIR="$DIST_ROOT/$DIST_NAME"

if [ ! -x "$MAVEN_HOME_DIR/bin/mvn" ]; then
  echo "[mvnw] Downloading $DIST_URL"
  mkdir -p "$DIST_ROOT"
  TMP_ZIP=$(mktemp)
  if command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1; then curl -fsSL -o "$TMP_ZIP" "$DIST_URL"; else wget -q -O "$TMP_ZIP" "$DIST_URL"; fi
  unzip -q -o "$TMP_ZIP" -d "$DIST_ROOT"
  rm -f "$TMP_ZIP"
  chmod +x "$MAVEN_HOME_DIR/bin/mvn"
fi

export MAVEN_PROJECTBASEDIR="$BASEDIR"
exec "$MAVEN_HOME_DIR/bin/mvn" -f "$BASEDIR/pom.xml" "$@"
